   "source": [
    "# Analysis of Cross-Dataset Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import ast"
   ]
  },
{
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "Advancements in biomedical signal monitoring techniques have contributed significantly to the early diagnosis and treatment of various medical conditions. Wearable systems are increasingly being used to monitor health conditions and provide real-time data on various physiological parameters. However, implementing deep learning advances into practical wearable systems often faces numerous challenges. These challenges span the entire lifecycle of a wearable device, from its data collection phase to its utilization by end-users. In our paper, we introduce MetaWearS, a purpose-built Meta-learning method for Wearable Systems that addresses the critical challenges of data scarcity and resource efficiency. Our approach reduces the data required for the initial training of the model and for the update process. Furthermore, our method incorporates an energy-efficient updating mechanism, and instead of retraining and transmitting the entire model, we update only a single vector, called prototype."
   ]
  }"import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import ast"
   ]
  },
{
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load and Preprocess Data\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell loads the results from the `results_meta_transfer.csv` file. It then preprocesses the `patients` and `finetune_patients` columns by converting the string representation of lists into actual lists. A new column `num_patients` is created to store the number of patients in the `patients` column. Finally, a random sample of 5 rows is displayed to inspect the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('../output/paper_results/results_meta_transfer.csv')\n",
    "df['num_patients'] = df['patients'].apply(lambda x: len(ast.literal_eval(x)))\n",
    "df['patients'] = df['patients'].apply(lambda x: ast.literal_eval(x))\n",
    "df['finetune_patients'] = df['finetune_patients'].apply(lambda x: ast.literal_eval(x))\n",
    "df.sample(n=5)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%% md\n"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## Compare per number of patients"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "condition = (df['patients'].apply(lambda x: x) == df['finetune_patients']) & (~df['skip_finetune']) & (~df['skip_base_learner'])\n",
    "df_patient_based = df[condition]\n",
    "grouped_data = df_patient_based.groupby('num_patients')['auc']\n",
    "\n",
    "mean_auc = grouped_data.mean()\n",
    "std_auc = grouped_data.std()\n",
    "print(\"mean \", mean_auc)\n",
    "print(\"std \", std_auc)\n",
    "num_patients = mean_auc.index\n",
    "\n",
    "# Creating the bar plot with error bars\n",
    "plt.bar(num_patients, mean_auc, yerr=std_auc, capsize=5, align='center')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Number of Patients')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Mean AUC')\n",
    "plt.title('Reuslts per number of patients in finetune set')\n",
    "plt.xticks(num_patients)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('./per_patient.png')\n"
   ]
  },
{
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Save Raw Data for Figure\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell saves the raw data used to generate the previous plot into a CSV file. This allows for reproducibility and further analysis of the results."
   ]
  },
{
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "output_csv_name = '../output/paper_results/figure5_epilepsy_raw.csv'\n",
    "df_patient_based[['num_patients', 'auc']].sort_values(by='num_patients').to_csv(output_csv_name, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully saved {len(df_patient_based)} contributing rows to {output_csv_name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mtick\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Assuming df_patient_based is already defined from previous steps\n",
    "\n",
    "# Increase global font size for all plot elements\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 14})\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare data: Group by 'num_patients' and collect all 'auc' values\n",
    "grouped = df_patient_based.groupby('num_patients')['auc']\n",
    "# Multiply by 100 to convert to percentage\n",
    "data_to_plot = [(group.values[:30]) * 100 for name, group in grouped]\n",
    "labels = [name for name, group in grouped]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define specific properties for the mean marker (Green Diamond)\n",
    "mean_props = dict(marker='D', markeredgecolor='black', markerfacecolor='#2ca02c', markersize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create the boxplot\n",
    "# showmeans=True enables the mean marker\n",
    "# whis=(0, 100) ensures whiskers cover the full range (no outliers)\n",
    "bp = plt.boxplot(data_to_plot, labels=labels, showfliers=False, showmeans=True, meanprops=mean_props, whis=(0, 100))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Overlay individual data points (jittered scatter plot)\n",
    "for i, data in enumerate(data_to_plot):\n",
    "    y = data\n",
    "    # Create x-coordinates with random jitter\n",
    "    x = np.random.normal(i + 1, 0.04, size=len(y))\n",
    "    # Plot points. We only add a label to the first one to avoid duplicate legend entries\n",
    "    plt.scatter(x, y, alpha=0.6, s=5, color='red', zorder=1, label='Individual Data' if i == 0 else \"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add a 'proxy artist' (an empty plot) to create a legend entry for the Mean\n",
    "plt.plot([], [], marker='D', color='#2ca02c', markeredgecolor='black', linestyle='None', markersize=12, label='Mean')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set labels and title with even larger fonts if needed\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Number of patients in meta-train', fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('AUC', fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.yticks(np.arange(20, 95, 10))\n",
    "# plt.title('Distribution of AUC per Number of Patients', fontsize=18)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add grid\n",
    "plt.grid(True, axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Format the Y-axis ticks as percentages\n",
    "plt.gca().yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add legend\n",
    "plt.legend(loc='lower right', frameon=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('./per_patient_boxplot_formatted.png')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%% md\n"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## Updating with new shots"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Figure X: Performance vs. Additional Shots from New Patients\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell generates a plot that corresponds to Figure X in the paper. The plot shows how the mean AUC changes as we add more shots from additional patients to the fine-tuning set. The x-axis represents the number of shots per patient, and the different lines represent different numbers of additional patients. The red 'X' marker shows the baseline performance without any new patients."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "condition = (df['patients'].apply(lambda x: x) != df['finetune_patients']) & (~df['skip_finetune']) & (~df['skip_base_learner'])\n",
    "df_updating_shots = df[condition]\n",
    "grouped = df_updating_shots.groupby(['num_patients', 'num_support'])['auc'].agg(['mean', 'std']).reset_index()\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Iterate through unique 'num_patients' values and plot mean with std margin for each\n",
    "for num_patients, group in grouped.groupby('num_patients'):\n",
    "    print(group['num_support'], group['mean'])\n",
    "    plt.plot(group['num_support'], group['mean'], label=f'Num Additional Patients: {num_patients -1}')\n",
    "additional_point_x = 0\n",
    "additional_point_y = grouped_data.mean().loc[1]\n",
    "plt.scatter(additional_point_x, additional_point_y, color='red', marker='X', label='w/o new patient')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Connect the additional point to all the plots\n",
    "for num_patients, group in grouped.groupby('num_patients'):\n",
    "    plt.plot([additional_point_x, group['num_support'].iloc[0]], [additional_point_y, group['mean'].iloc[0]], color='gray', linestyle='dashed')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Shots per Patient')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Mean AUC')\n",
    "plt.title('Results with new shots from other patients than finetune')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show the plot\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.savefig('output/notebook_outputs/new_shot.png')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%% md\n"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## Ablation study"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Figure 9c and 9d: Ablation Study\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell generates a plot that corresponds to Figure 9c and 9d in the paper. The plot shows the results of an ablation study, comparing the performance of the full meta-transfer learning model with two ablated versions:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **w/o Finetune**: The model is not fine-tuned on the target patient data.\n",
    "- **w/o Base Learner**: The model is trained from scratch on the target patient data, without using the pre-trained base learner."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# plt.figure()\n",
    "df_skip_finetune = df[df['skip_finetune']]\n",
    "df_skip_base_learner = df[df['skip_base_learner']]\n",
    "for num_patient_in_FT in [1,3]:\n",
    "    plt.figure()\n",
    "    df_skip_finetune[df_skip_finetune['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT].groupby('num_support')['auc'].mean().plot(label='w/o Finetune')\n",
    "    skip_BL_value = df_skip_base_learner[df_skip_base_learner['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT].groupby('num_support')['auc'].mean().to_list()\n",
    "    plt.plot([1, 3, 5, 10, 15, 20], skip_BL_value * 6, label='w/o Base Learner')\n",
    "    plt.plot([1, 3, 5, 10, 15, 20],[grouped_data.mean().loc[num_patient_in_FT]] * 6, label='Full Meta-transfer learning')\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.xlabel('Shots per Patient')\n",
    "    plt.ylabel('Mean AUC')\n",
    "    plt.title('Ablation Study to compare the result without Finetune OR without Base-leraner\\n{} patients present in the finetune set'.format(num_patient_in_FT))\n",
    "    plt.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Show the plot\n",
    "    plt.grid(True)\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.savefig('output/notebook_outputs/Ablation_study_{}.png'.format(num_patient_in_FT))"
   ]
  },
{
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Statistical Significance Tests\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cells perform independent two-sample t-tests to determine if the differences in performance observed in the ablation study are statistically significant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_skip_finetune[df_skip_finetune['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT].groupby('num_support')['auc'].std()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def define_type(row):\n",
    "    if row['skip_base_learner']:\n",
    "        return 'Without Base Learner'\n",
    "    elif row['skip_finetune']:\n",
    "        # Format num_support as integer for cleaner output (e.g., \"5\" instead of \"5.0\")\n",
    "        shots = int(row['num_support'])\n",
    "        return f\"Without Fine Tune {shots}\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Proposed'\n",
    "\n",
    "df_skip_finetune = df[df['skip_finetune']]\n",
    "df_skip_base_learner = df[df['skip_base_learner']]\n",
    "num_patient_in_FT = 3\n",
    "df_skip_finetune = df_skip_finetune[df_skip_finetune['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT]\n",
    "skip_BL_value = df_skip_base_learner[df_skip_base_learner['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT]\n",
    "proposed_ablation = df_patient_based[df_patient_based['num_patients'] == num_patient_in_FT]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_ablation_combined = pd.concat([df_skip_finetune, skip_BL_value, proposed_ablation], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "df_ablation_combined = df_ablation_combined[['auc', 'num_support', 'skip_base_learner','skip_finetune']]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply the function to create the 'type' column\n",
    "df_ablation_combined['type'] = df_ablation_combined.apply(define_type, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_ablation_combined = df_ablation_combined[['auc', 'type']]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Save to CSV\n",
    "output_csv_name = './ablation_study_combined.csv'\n",
    "df_ablation_combined.to_csv(output_csv_name, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully saved {len(df_ablation_combined)} rows to {output_csv_name}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
    "data2 = df_skip_base_learner[df_skip_base_learner['num_patients'] == 3]['auc'].to_list()\n",
    "data1 = df_patient_based[df_patient_based['num_patients'] == 3]['auc'].to_list()\n",
    "t_stat, p_value = stats.ttest_ind(data1, data2, equal_var=True)  # Assuming unequal variances\\\n",
    "t_stat, p_value"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data3 = df_skip_finetune[(df_skip_finetune['num_patients'] == 3) & (df_skip_finetune['num_support'] == 20)]['auc'].to_list()\n",
    "t_stat, p_value = stats.ttest_ind(data1, data3, equal_var=True)  # Assuming unequal variances\\\n",
    "t_stat, p_value"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Noise resiliance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Figure 9a: Noise Resilience\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell generates a box plot that corresponds to Figure 9a in the paper. The plot shows the performance of the model in terms of AUC under different Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) levels. This analysis evaluates the model's robustness to noise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from matplotlib.lines import Line2D\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Read the CSV file\n",
    "# Replace 'your_file_name.csv' with the actual name of your file containing the SNR data\n",
    "file_path = '../output/paper_results/results_noisy.csv' \n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(file_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['auc'] = df['auc'] * 100\n",
    "df['auc'] = 87.7 - df['auc']\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Filter data\n",
    "# Remove rows where snr is 0.0001 or 1\n",
    "df_filtered = df[~df['snr'].isin([0.0001, 1, 1000])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Setup the plot\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n",
    "# Set consistent global font size\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 14})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define marker properties for the mean (Green Diamond)\n",
    "mean_props = dict(marker='D', markeredgecolor='black', markerfacecolor='#2ca02c', markersize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Create the Box Plot\n",
    "# showfliers=False prevents outlier points from being plotted by the boxplot itself,\n",
    "# avoiding duplication with the strip plot points.\n",
    "ax = sns.boxplot(\n",
    "    x='snr',\n",
    "    y='auc',\n",
    "    data=df_filtered,\n",
    "    showmeans=True,\n",
    "    meanprops=mean_props,\n",
    "    palette=\"Set2\",\n",
    "    showfliers=False \n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Overlay individual data points\n",
    "# sns.stripplot adds the jittered points on top of the boxes\n",
    "sns.stripplot(\n",
    "    x='snr',\n",
    "    y='auc',\n",
    "    data=df_filtered,\n",
    "    color='red',\n",
    "    size=3,\n",
    "    jitter=True,\n",
    "    alpha=0.6,\n",
    "    zorder=3\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 6. Create custom legend\n",
    "# Define proxy artists for the legend entries\n",
    "legend_elements = [\n",
    "    Line2D([0], [0], color='#2ca02c', marker='D', linestyle='None',\n",
    "           markeredgecolor='black', markersize=8, label='Mean'),\n",
    "    Line2D([0], [0], marker='.', color='w', label='Individual Data',\n",
    "           markerfacecolor='red', markersize=10, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add legend to the plot\n",
    "plt.legend(handles=legend_elements, loc='upper right', frameon=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 7. Formatting\n",
    "plt.xlabel('SNR (dB)', fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('AUC', fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "plt.gca().yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter(decimals=0))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 8. Save and Show\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('output/notebook_outputs/snr_boxplot_filtered.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Select only 'snr' and 'auc' columns\n",
    "output_df = df_filtered[['snr', 'auc']]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save to CSV\n",
    "# index=False ensures the row numbers are not saved as a separate column\n",
    "output_csv_name = 'output/notebook_outputs/snr_auc_results.csv'\n",
    "output_df.to_csv(output_csv_name, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully saved {len(output_df)} rows to {output_csv_name}\")"
   ]
  }
